# Netlify security headers, applied to every route.
#
# Two directives here are load-bearing for the 3D view, and neither is
# exercised by `npm run dev` (the dev server sends no CSP at all):
#   - connect-src blob:      GLTFLoader unpacks each model's embedded textures
#                            into blob: URLs and reads them back with
#                            ImageBitmapLoader, i.e. fetch() — which connect-src
#                            governs, not img-src. Blocking it rejects the whole
#                            model, not just the texture, so every textured part
#                            silently degrades to a grey box.
#   - script-src 'wasm-unsafe-eval'
#                            motherboard.glb requires EXT_meshopt_compression,
#                            whose decoder compiles WebAssembly. This token
#                            permits WASM only — it does NOT allow JS eval().
# Covered by src/tests/cspHeaders.test.js.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' blob: https://igeggndtnmdpauxovnwv.supabase.co; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'
